# Day 14/50 — Transactions

Imagine transferring money to someone.

The amount should leave one account and reach the other. 
Both actions are connected
If one happens but the other fails, something goes wrong.

That's why databases use **transactions**

A transaction is a group of operations treated as one logical unit either all the operations are completed successfully, or the changes are rolled back

No half-finished operations , no incomplete updates.

And isn't that interesting?

Some things only make sense when every part of them works together
Completing just one half doesn't mean the task is done.

**Because sometimes, it's not about starting something. It's about making sure it reaches completion.**
